# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase Auth configuration (all values are read from the runtime env and
# inlined into both the server and the browser bundle by Next.js).
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) for local development, and set the same
# variables in the hosting provider (Vercel → Project → Environment Variables).
#
# Every NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* value below is optional at build time: when a
# variable is missing the app falls back to the documented fallback project and
# says so in the console + in the in-app diagnostics panel. In production, set
# them all (an incomplete set is the most common cause of
# `auth/invalid-api-key`, `auth/configuration-not-found` and redirect failures).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# "firebase" → real Firebase Auth · "demo" → on-device gateway · "auto" → Firebase
# when the config below is complete, demo otherwise. Default when unset: demo.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_BACKEND=firebase

NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyAbb9aCsOfMkw9G5H0L58LSkbsONhix51k
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=agriculture-intelligente-7873e.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=agriculture-intelligente-7873e
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=agriculture-intelligente-7873e.firebasestorage.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=213483282746
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:213483282746:web:badde539687095497a7003
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-VKD4SWJLNJ

# Firebase Console → Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains must list
# every origin the app is served from, including the Arena preview host
# (*.e2b.app) and http://localhost:3000 for local development.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI assistant — 3-stage resilient chain behind /api/assistant (server-only
# secrets; NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix so they are never inlined into the browser
# bundle).
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY       → Google AI Studio → Get API key (aistudio.google.com/apikey)
#                        FALLBACK LLM (Stage 2): gemini-3.6 by default
#                        (→ 2.5-flash → 2.0-flash-exp when an id is retired;
#                        pin another id with GEMINI_MODEL below) via
#                        https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/<model>:generateContent
#                        under ONE shared 18 s AbortController deadline for the
#                        whole model chain (a full Arabic answer needs 10–15 s on
#                        a cold Flash model; 9 s aborted healthy generations).
#                        It receives the system instruction, the user query,
#                        the profile context (wilaya, crop, role) and — when a
#                        leaf photo was sent — the photo ITSELF (inlineData)
#                        plus the Step 1 MobileNetV2 reference diagnosis
#                        (disease label, confidence score, candidate diseases):
#                        Gemini inspects the image, evaluates the MobileNetV2
#                        reference and generates the final structured
#                        diagnosis report (source: "hybrid"). When MobileNetV2
#                        fails, Gemini inspects the raw image independently;
#                        when EVERY LLM stage fails, a structured reply is
#                        built directly from MobileNetV2's findings
#                        (source: "direct").
#                        Gemini runs SECOND: the Hugging Face router below is
#                        the PRIMARY LLM and is always called first — Gemini
#                        answers only when that stage fails or is unconfigured.
#                        Multi-key rotation: EVERY variable starting with
#                        GEMINI_API_KEY participates — GEMINI_API_KEY, the
#                        GEMINI_API_KEYS comma-separated pool, and numbered
#                        variants (GEMINI_API_KEY_1, GEMINI_API_KEY_2, …).
#                        They are combined, trimmed and deduplicated into one
#                        pool. On rate-limit errors (HTTP 429,
#                        RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED, quota limit) the route rotates to
#                        the next key and retries until one answers or all
#                        keys are exhausted, the built-in formatter answers
#                        locally. A successful answer returns HTTP 200
#                        { source: "llm" } (source: "hybrid" when it ships
#                        with a diagnosis).
#
# GEMINI_MODEL (OPTIONAL, server-only) — Stage 2 (FALLBACK) model id.
#                        Default: gemini-3.6. Pin any other
#                        generateContent-capable id, e.g.
#                        GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash-exp. A retired/mistyped
#                        id still walks the built-in fallback chain
#                        (gemini-2.5-flash → gemini-2.0-flash-exp), so an
#                        override can never brick the stage. Blank or unset =
#                        the gemini-3.6 default.
#
# HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY  → Hugging Face → Settings → Access Tokens. Create a
#                        fine-grained token and tick "Make calls to Inference
#                        Providers" (a plain read token 401/403s on the router).
#                        Powers BOTH vision and the PRIMARY LLM (Stage 1):
#                        Step 1 — PlantVillage leaf-disease vision classifier
#                        on the hf-inference provider:
#                        linkanjarad/mobilenet_v2_1.0_224-plant-disease-
#                        identification (MobileNetV2 — the single clean
#                        default; the 400-prone cascade ids are removed.
#                        Pin a replacement with HF_VISION_MODEL).
#                        Stage 1 (PRIMARY LLM) — concise Arabic reply from an
#                        open, non-gated, lightweight Qwen chain through the
#                        official Inference Providers router
#                        https://router.huggingface.co/v1/chat/completions
#                        (Qwen/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 → Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct
#                        → Qwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct). The router picks a live
#                        provider per model and the account's monthly free
#                        Inference Providers credits apply. If every LLM is
#                        unavailable, a built-in formatter still answers from
#                        the Step 1 diagnosis (source: "direct", never a 500).
#                        HF_TOKEN (Hugging Face's own variable name) is
#                        honoured as an alias when HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY is
#                        unset/blank. With neither set, Step 1 and Stage 1 are
#                        skipped instantly (no request, no error, no delay) and
#                        the Gemini fallback answers when it is configured.
#
# Set at least one of the two keys on the server at runtime (including on
# Vercel): each stage is optional and degrades to the next one. Only when BOTH
# keys are missing/blank does the route answer HTTP 503 with code MISSING_KEYS.
# Every other outcome answers HTTP 200: upstream AI failures degrade to
# built-in direct replies ({ source: "direct" }) — the API never returns 500.
# Never expose these secrets with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# HF_LEAF_DETECT_MODELS (OPTIONAL, server-only) — Step 0 "Detection &
#                        Cropping" detector chain, tried in order. Step 0
#                        runs an open-source object detector BEFORE the
#                        PlantVillage classifier: the leaf is localised, the
#                        photo is cropped with sharp and ONLY the cropped
#                        pixels are forwarded to Step 1 (background noise —
#                        hands, soil, pots — never reaches the classifier).
#                        Default detector (open weights, free hf-inference
#                        tier): facebook/detr-resnet-50 (COCO DETR-ResNet-50,
#                        plant/leaf-labelled boxes only — the obsolete
#                        fine-tuned PlantDoc checkpoint is gone). Override
#                        with a comma-separated list of Hub ids, e.g.:
#                        HF_LEAF_DETECT_MODELS=myorg/leaf-detector
#                        When the detector is unavailable or finds no leaf,
#                        the untouched original frame is classified instead
#                        (the outcome is reported in the `preprocessing`
#                        field of the API response).
#
# HF_VISION_MODEL (OPTIONAL, server-only) — Step 1 PlantVillage classifier,
#                        a single Hub id that replaces the default
#                        linkanjarad/mobilenet_v2_1.0_224-plant-disease-
#                        identification (e.g. a self-hosted/retrained
#                        checkpoint). Unset = the clean MobileNetV2 default.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEYS=
GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
GEMINI_API_KEY_3=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6
HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=
HF_LEAF_DETECT_MODELS=
HF_VISION_MODEL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REMOVED — CodeCraft vision engine (CODECRAFT_API_KEY / CODECRAFT_BASE_URL /
# CODECRAFT_VISION_MODEL). The streamlined diagnostic pipeline routes Step 1
# DIRECTLY to the MobileNetV2 PlantVillage classifier on Hugging Face; the
# CodeCraft gateway is no longer called (its WAF 403 stalls and the extra
# round-trip only added latency). Leftover CODECRAFT_* variables in an
# existing environment are ignored and can be deleted.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
